+-  WHY THE ORACLE RUNS IT. RexxInstructionOptions::execute
+-  (interpreter/instructions/OptionsInstruction.cpp) traces the instruction and
+-  evaluates its expression as a string, so an error inside that expression still
+-  raises. The word scan that would act on the resulting string sits inside
+-  #ifdef _DEBUG, under a comment saying processing is currently disabled. So in
+-  the build this project measures against, an OPTIONS instruction whose
+-  expression evaluates has no effect beyond the tracing and the interactive
+-  pause that execute performs for it, and refusing the program is an
+-  over-refusal in the sense the directives section above defines: it rejects a
+-  program the oracle runs.
